Project Name: E-commerce Product Review & Rating System
Author: Abdelaziz Mohamed (Team Lead & System Analyst)
Methodology: Rapid Application Development (RAD)
Document Context: Phase 1 - Requirements Determination & Stakeholder Analysis

--------------------------------------------------
1. INTERVIEW OPINION
--------------------------------------------------

Based on the qualitative feedback gathered during stakeholder interviews with store managers, vendors, and frequent shoppers:
- Dissatisfaction with Current Feedback Mechanics: Stakeholders universally express that open, unmoderated text comment sections harm the store's overall reputation. Unverified feedback creates noise rather than actionable insight.
- Value of Authenticity & Visual Proof: Interviewees strongly agree that restricting feedback to Verified Buyers—accompanied by authentic photos and videos—is the single most effective way to restore buyer confidence and drive purchase conversions.
- Expectation of Public Accountability: Store managers emphasize that responding publicly to critical feedback demonstrates accountability and long-term commitment to customer service, turning negative experiences into trust-building opportunities.

--------------------------------------------------
2. INTERVIEW FEELINGS
--------------------------------------------------

During the requirement-gathering sessions, clear emotional tones and sentiment dynamics were identified across different user groups:
- Frustration & Vulnerability: Store owners and genuine vendors expressed high levels of frustration regarding fake reviews, competitor spam, and malicious low ratings that unfairly damage product rankings and sales.
- Hesitation & Cart Abandonment Anxiety: Shoppers conveyed skepticism and anxiety when encountering products without clear, verified ratings, often resulting in cart abandonment out of fear of receiving substandard goods.
- Optimism & Relief Toward Automation: Both administrative and technical stakeholders showed strong enthusiasm for integrating Python-based automated moderation (NLTK/TextBlob) and Power BI analytics, anticipating immediate relief from manual review inspection.

--------------------------------------------------
3. CURRENT STATE OF THE SYSTEM (AS-IS STATE)
--------------------------------------------------

The analysis of the legacy e-commerce feedback module revealed several operational and technical bottlenecks:
- Unrestricted & Unverified Access: Any visitor (including guest users without purchase history) can post comments, leading to a high incidence of spam and untraceable feedback.
- Purely Manual Moderation Workflow: Customer support staff manually review, approve, or delete every submitted comment, creating severe administrative backlogs and delaying legitimate review publications.
- Basic Text-Only Format: The existing module lacks structured 1-to-5 star rating metrics, media upload capabilities (images/videos), or custom feedback criteria (e.g., product fit, shipping speed).
- Zero Analytical Integration: Review text remains trapped in unindexed database columns without any connection to reporting platforms or business intelligence tools.

--------------------------------------------------
4. SYSTEM GOALS (TO-BE ARCHITECTURE)
--------------------------------------------------

To address the diagnostic findings, the upcoming E-commerce Product Review & Rating System is engineered to achieve the following target objectives prior to the January 1st deadline:
- 100% Verified Buyer Restrictions: Implement API logic that validates user transaction history against order records before granting review submission permissions.
- Automated Python Moderation & Sentiment Analysis: Deploy NLTK and TextBlob automated filtering scripts to block profanity, detect spam patterns, and route flagged negative feedback to support teams instantly.
- Rich Multi-Criteria Review Interface: Build a modern React front-end component supporting 1-to-5 star ratings, photo/video evidence uploads, and multi-attribute scoring.
- Power BI Executive Dashboards: Integrate SQL Server data with Power BI to provide management with real-time analytics on product quality trends, return risk alerts, and customer sentiment metrics.
- Optimal Performance Standards: Maintain sub-second widget load times (<= 0.5s) to ensure zero impact on general store loading speed
